


   =====( KillOldMail V1.00 )========================================


        Trion 'KillOldMail' Utility.

        (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '94-'97. All rights reserved.

        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


   This is a little programm to delete mail from your outbound
   directory for systems that didn't poll your system in a while.
   This will keep your outbound from filling completely if
   someone 'forgets' to call a few weeks .. if someone doesn't
   call a while he probably doesn't want the old mail anyway.

   You call it with the number of days the mail must be old to
   delete it.
   The number of days must be greater then 3 .. this was done
   to prevent errors in use.


   Use:   KillOldMail [outbound] <days> [-Q]         (days > 3)

   The default path of the outbound is "trion:outbound/" but if
   you use an other directory in the trionrm.cfg you have
   to specify it on the command line.
   Also you can use the -Q flag to make the utilty 'Quiet',
   or else it will give a summary of files it removes.

   It actually deletes files with names ending with:

   .PKT , .MO? , .TU? , .WE? , .TH? , .FR? , .SA? , .SU?


   You could use this utility in the maintenance script
   but in the default BBS it isn't used.



